<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korean won hits six-year low of 846.50.</title>
<headline>South Korean won hits six-year low of 846.50.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Korean won fell to a six-year low of 846.50 in early morning trading on Thursday, pressured by strong import settlements, traders said.</p>
<p>This was the lowest level seen since the market averaging system was introduced in March 1990.  </p>
<p>The won is expected to fall further without central bank support, dealers said.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
